,9,9,3,3,3],[1,1,1,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,3,3,3],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[1,1,1,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9],[9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,8,9,9,9]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"The rule was not at fault. The program crashed only because `collections` was used without being imported inside the sandbox. The fix is to add `import collections` at the top of `transform`.\n\n## The rule\n\n**What the input contains**\n- **Legend strip.** The rows containing colour 5 (rows 0–5) form a strip at the top. It holds four panels. Each panel is a block of 0s with one coloured marker column on either its left or its right.\n- **Canvas.** Everything below the strip is a canvas with a background colour, several solid blocks, and one square of colour 8.\n\n**What the output is**\n- The output is the canvas alone, so the legend strip is removed.\n- From the 8 square, four beams start: up, down, left and right. Each beam is as wide as the square.\n\n**How a beam moves**\n- A beam advances one cell at a time and paints 8 as it goes.\n- When the next position would overlap a coloured block, the beam turns in place.\n  - If that colour's marker is on the **left** of its 0-block, the beam turns left relative to its direction of travel.\n  - If the marker is on the **right**, it turns right.\n  - Because it turns before entering, the corner of the path sits right against the block.\n- A beam stops when it leaves the grid, or when it hits a colour that is not in the legend.\n\n## Checking it against the demonstrations\n\n**Pair 1**\n- The up beam meets nothing and runs to the top edge.\n- The left beam hits colour 1 (marker left) and turns from west to south.\n- Both the down beam and that turned beam hit colour 2 (marker left) and turn east to the edge.\n- The right beam hits colour 4 (marker left) and turns north to the edge.\n\n**Pair 2**\n- Colour 2 has its marker on the right, so the left beam turns north.\n- The right beam hits colour 3 (left) and turns north, then hits colour 6 (right) and turns east to the edge.\n\n**Pair 3**\n- The up beam hits colour 3 (marker left) and turns west to the edge. This gives rows 4–5 of the output.\n- The left beam hits colour 2 (marker right) and turns north. This gives columns 3–4.\n- The down beam hits colour 4. Here colour 4's marker sits on the *right* of its 0s, so the beam turns west. It then hits colour 2 (right) and turns north, giving columns 3–4 down to row 15.\n- The right beam hits colour 6 (marker left) and turns north. This gives columns 18–19.\n\n## Applying it to the test input\n- The strip ends at row 5, so the canvas is rows 6–29 (24 rows).\n- The 8 square is 3×3, so every beam is 3 cells wide.\n- Legend: 1 → left, 3 → right, 2 → left, 4 → left.\n- The program uses the same procedure as above on this canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    import collections\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    # header: rows containing colour 5\n    rows5 = [y for y in range(H) if (g[y] == 5).any()]\n    top = max(rows5) + 1\n    header = g[:top]\n    # legend: colour -> turn ('L' or 'R') by which side of the 0-block the marker sits\n    legend = {}\n    for comp in components(header == 0):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(comp)\n        yc = y0\n        if x0 - 1 >= 0 and header[yc, x0 - 1] not in (0, 5):\n            legend[int(header[yc, x0 - 1])] = 'L'\n        if x1 + 1 < W and header[yc, x1 + 1] not in (0, 5):\n            legend[int(header[yc, x1 + 1])] = 'R'\n    body = g[top:].copy()\n    emit(body, \"Cut away the legend strip; the canvas below is the working grid.\")\n    bg = background(body)\n    h, w = body.shape\n    ys, xs = np.where(body == 8)\n    sy0, sx0, sy1, sx1 = ys.min(), xs.min(), ys.max(), xs.max()\n    bh, bw = sy1 - sy0 + 1, sx1 - sx0 + 1\n    out = body.copy()\n\n    def blocker(y, x):\n        if y < 0 or x < 0 or y + bh > h or x + bw > w:\n            return 'edge'\n        blk = body[y:y + bh, x:x + bw]\n        vals = [int(v) for v in blk.ravel() if v != bg and v != 8]\n        if vals:\n            return collections.Counter(vals).most_common(1)[0][0]\n        return None\n\n    names = {(-1, 0): \"up\", (1, 0): \"down\", (0, -1): \"left\", (0, 1): \"right\"}\n    for d0 in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n        y, x = sy0, sx0\n        dy, dx = d0\n        steps = 0\n        while steps < 500:\n            steps += 1\n            ny, nx = y + dy, x + dx\n            b = blocker(ny, nx)\n            if b is None:\n                y, x = ny, nx\n                out[y:y + bh, x:x + bw] = 8\n                continue\n            if b == 'edge':\n                break\n            t = legend.get(int(b))\n            if t is None:\n                break\n            if t == 'L':\n                dy, dx = -dx, dy\n            else:\n                dy, dx = dx, -dy\n        emit(out, f\"Shoot the beam {names[d0]} from the 8 square, turning at each block per the legend side, until it leaves the grid.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final canvas with all 8 paths drawn.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"It holds four panels."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each panel is a block of 0s with one coloured marker column on either its left or its right."}],"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Legend strip.** The rows containing colour 5 (rows 0–5) form a strip at the top."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The output is the canvas alone, so the legend strip is removed."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Legend: 1 → left, 3 → right, 2 → left, 4 → left."}],"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Because it turns before entering, the corner of the path sits right against the block."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Final canvas with all 8 paths drawn."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- From the 8 square, four beams start: up, down, left and right."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each beam is as wide as the square."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How a beam moves**"}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- When the next position would overlap a coloured block, the beam turns in place."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"b0b4c77487fc64eb15c8e2209ad912814d567dc69d404d27321a7962cb07e118","task_sha256":"9bb5f8f2edd21ab4231234c11c5f2e08057f6091e09887aff5e71402b3612dec","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
